        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336845",
          "text": "<p>Correct expression tor UDP&nbsp;user datagram length is</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>length of UDP = length of IP- length of IP header's</li>\n    <li>length of UDP= length of UDP-length of UDP header's</li>\n    <li>length of UDP = length of IP+length of IP header's</li>\n    <li>length of UDP = length of UDP+length of UDP header's</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,udp",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336844",
          "text": "<p>In binary search tree which traversal is used for getting ascending order values ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Inorder</li>\n    <li>Preorder</li>\n    <li>Postorder</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,data-structures,binary-search-tree,tree-traversal",
          "category": "Data Structures"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336843",
          "text": "<p>The automaton which allows transformation to a new state without consuming any input symbols :&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$NFA$</li>\n    <li>$DFA$</li>\n    <li>$NFA - 1$</li>\n    <li>All of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,finite-automata",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336842",
          "text": "<p>Complement of a $DFA$ can be obtained by :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>making starting state as final state.</li>\n    <li>make final as a starting state.</li>\n    <li>making final states non-final and non-final as final.</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,finite-automata",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336841",
          "text": "<p>Concatenation Operation refers to which of the following set operations :&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Union</li>\n    <li>Dot</li>\n    <li>Kleene</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,finite-automata",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336840",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements is true ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Melay and Moore machines are language acceptors.</li>\n    <li>Finite State automata is language translator.</li>\n    <li>NPDA is more powerful than DPDA.</li>\n    <li>Melay machine is more powerful than Moore machine.</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,dpda,npda",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336839",
          "text": "<p>If file size is large and if it is to be accessed randomly then which of the following allocation strategy should be best to use in a system?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Linked allocation</li>\n    <li>Indexed allocation</li>\n    <li>Contiguous allocation</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system,file-system",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336838",
          "text": "<p>Microprocessors are used in which generation of computers?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>I – st&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Generation</li>\n    <li>II – nd&nbsp;Generation</li>\n    <li>III – rd&nbsp;Generation</li>\n    <li>IV – th&nbsp;Generation</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,non-gatecse,microprocessors",
          "category": "Digital Signal Processing"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336837",
          "text": "<p>Operating System maintains the page table for :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>each process</li>\n    <li>each thread</li>\n    <li>each instruction</li>\n    <li>each address</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system,paging,threads",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336836",
          "text": "<p>The function &nbsp;$f\\left ( x \\right )=\\dfrac{x^{2}-1}{x-1}$ at $x=1$ is&nbsp;:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Continuous and differentiable</li>\n    <li>Continuous but not differentiable</li>\n    <li>Differentiable but not continuous</li>\n    <li>Neither continuous nor differentiable</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,engineering-mathematics,calculus,continuity",
          "category": "Calculus"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336835",
          "text": "<p>Closed - Loop control mechanism try to :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Remove congestion after it occurs</li>\n    <li>Remove congestion after sometime</li>\n    <li>Prevent congestion before it occurs</li>\n    <li>Prevent congestion before sending packets</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,congestion-control",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336834",
          "text": "<p>In classless addressing, there are no classes but addresses are still granted in :&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Codes</li>\n    <li>Blocks</li>\n    <li>IPs</li>\n    <li>Sizes</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,ip-addressing,subnetting",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336833",
          "text": "<p>Which multiple access technique is used by $\\text{IEEE&nbsp; } 802.11$ standard for wireless $\\text{LAN}$ ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$\\text{CDMA}$</li>\n    <li>$\\text{CSMA/CA}$</li>\n    <li>$\\text{ALOHA}$</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,csma-ca",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336832",
          "text": "<p>$PGP$ encrypts data by using a block cipher called :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>international data encryption algorithm</li>\n    <li>private data encryption algorithm</li>\n    <li>internet data encryption algorithm</li>\n    <li>none of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,network-security",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336831",
          "text": "<p>If $L1$ and $L2$ are regular sets then intersection of these two will be :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Regular</li>\n    <li>Non Regular</li>\n    <li>Recursive</li>\n    <li>Non Recursive</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,regular-language",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336830",
          "text": "<p>The smallest integer that can be represented by an $8$-bit number in $2$'s&nbsp;complement form is :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$-256$</li>\n    <li>$-128$</li>\n    <li>$-127$</li>\n    <li>$0$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,digital-logic,number-system",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336829",
          "text": "<p>Non-contiguous memory allocation splits program into blocks of memory called ________ that can be loaded in non-adjacent holes in main memory.</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Pages</li>\n    <li>Frames</li>\n    <li>Partition</li>\n    <li>Segments</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system,page-replacement,segmentation",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336828",
          "text": "<p>In a full binary tree number of nodes is $63$ then the height of the tree is :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$2$</li>\n    <li>$4$</li>\n    <li>$3$</li>\n    <li>$6$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "X",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,data-structures,binary-tree",
          "category": "Data Structures"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336827",
          "text": "<p>Let $P, Q, R$ be a regular expression over $\\Sigma$. If $P$ does not contain null string, then $R=Q+RP$ has a unique solution ___________ .</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$Q^{*}P$</li>\n    <li>$QP^{*}$</li>\n    <li>$Q^{*}P^{*}$</li>\n    <li>$\\left (&nbsp;P^{*}O^{*} \\right)^{*}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,regular-expression",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336826",
          "text": "<p>Total number of simple graphs that can be drawn using six vertices are:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$2^{15}$</li>\n    <li>$2^{14}$</li>\n    <li>$2^{13}$</li>\n    <li>$2^{12}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,discrete-mathematics,graph-theory",
          "category": "Graph Theory"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336825",
          "text": "<p>The $2-3-4$ tree is a self-balancing data structure, which is also called :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$2-4$ tree</li>\n    <li>$B+$ tree</li>\n    <li>$B-$ tree</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,databases,b-tree",
          "category": "Databases"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336824",
          "text": "<p>Which type of algorithm is used to solve the \"$8$ Queens\" problem ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Greedy</li>\n    <li>Dynamic</li>\n    <li>Divide and conquer</li>\n    <li>Backtracking</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,algorithms,backtracking,easy",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336823",
          "text": "<p>A $3.5$ inch micro floppy high density disk contains the data _________ .</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$720 \\: MB$</li>\n    <li>$1.44 \\: MB$</li>\n    <li>$720 \\: KB$</li>\n    <li>$1.44 \\: KB$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,co-and-architecture,disk",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336822",
          "text": "<p>A subnet mask in class $C$ can have _____________ $1$’s&nbsp;with the remaining bits $0$’s.</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$10$</li>\n    <li>$24$</li>\n    <li>$12$</li>\n    <li>$7$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,subnetting,ip-addressing",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336821",
          "text": "<p>What is the value of acknowledgement field in a segment</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Number of previous bytes to receive</li>\n    <li>Total number of bytes to receive</li>\n    <li>Number of next bytes to receive</li>\n    <li>Sequence of zero's and one's</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,segmentation",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336820",
          "text": "<p>The number $(25)_6$, in base $6$ is equivalent to _________ in binary number system.</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$11001$</li>\n    <li>$10001$</li>\n    <li>$11000$</li>\n    <li>$10000$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,digital-logic,number-system",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336819",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following is a class $B$ host address ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$230.0.0.0$</li>\n    <li>$130.4.5.6$</li>\n    <li>$230.7.6.5$</li>\n    <li>$30.4.5.6$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,network-addressing,ip-addressing",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336818",
          "text": "<p>There is a need to create a network that has $5$ subnets, each with at least $16$ hosts. Which one is used as classful subnet mask ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$255.255.255.192$</li>\n    <li>$255.255.255.248$</li>\n    <li>$255.255.255.240$</li>\n    <li>$255.255.255.224$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,network-addressing,subnetting",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336817",
          "text": "<p>What is Compaction ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>a technique for overcoming internal fragmentation</li>\n    <li>a paging technique</li>\n    <li>a technique for overcoming external fragmentation</li>\n    <li>a technique for overcoming fatal error</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system,fragmentation",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336816",
          "text": "<p>How can we set a Cookie visibility scope to local storage ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$\\$$</li>\n    <li>$\\%$</li>\n    <li>$/$</li>\n    <li>All of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,non-gatecse,web-technologies",
          "category": "Web Technologies"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336815",
          "text": "<p>A finite automaton accepts which type of language :&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Type $0$</li>\n    <li>Type $1$</li>\n    <li>Type $2$</li>\n    <li>Type $3$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,identify-class-language,finite-automata",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336814",
          "text": "<p>Which NetWare protocol provides link - state routing ?&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$NLSP$</li>\n    <li>$RIP$</li>\n    <li>$SAP$</li>\n    <li>$NCP$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,routing,network-protocols",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336813",
          "text": "<p>Which layer connects the network support layers and user support layers ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>transport layer</li>\n    <li>network layer</li>\n    <li>data link layer</li>\n    <li>session layer</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,network-layer,transport-layer",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336812",
          "text": "<p>Process is in a ready state _______ .</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>when process is scheduled to run after some execution</li>\n    <li>when process is unable to run until some task has been completed</li>\n    <li>when process is using the $CPU$</li>\n    <li>none of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system,process-scheduling",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336811",
          "text": "<p>$\\left (0+ \\varepsilon \\right) \\left (1+ \\varepsilon \\right)$ represents :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$\\left \\{0,1,01,\\varepsilon &nbsp;\\right \\}$</li>\n    <li>$\\left \\{0,1,\\varepsilon &nbsp;\\right \\}$</li>\n    <li>$\\left \\{0,1,01, 11, 00 ,10,\\varepsilon &nbsp;\\right \\}$</li>\n    <li>$\\left \\{0,1,&nbsp; \\right \\}$</li>\n</ol>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,regular-expression",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336810",
          "text": "<p>The average search time of hashing, with linear probing will be less if the load factor :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>is far less than $1$</li>\n    <li>equals $1$</li>\n    <li>is far greater than $1$</li>\n    <li>none of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,algorithms,hashing",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336809",
          "text": "<p>How many times the word \"PROCESS\" will be printed when executing the following program ?</p>\n\n<pre class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\" data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\">\nmain(){\n    printf(\"PROCESS\");\n    fflush();\n    fork();\n    fork();\n}</pre>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$8$</li>\n    <li>$4$</li>\n    <li>$6$</li>\n    <li>$7$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "X",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system,system-calls",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336808",
          "text": "<p>If a planner graph, having $25$ vertices divides the plane into $17$ different regions. Then how many edges are used to connect the vertices in this graph.</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$20$</li>\n    <li>$30$</li>\n    <li>$40$</li>\n    <li>$50$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,discrete-mathematics,graph-theory,graph-planarity",
          "category": "Graph Theory"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336807",
          "text": "<p>Merge sort uses :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Divide-and-conquer</li>\n    <li>Backtracking</li>\n    <li>Heuristic approach</li>\n    <li>Greedy approach</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,algorithms,sorting,merge-sort,divide-and-conquer",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336806",
          "text": "<p>What is the relation between $DFA$ and $NFA$ on the basis of computational power ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$DFA$ &gt; $NFA$</li>\n    <li>$NFA$ &gt; $DFA$</li>\n    <li>Equal</li>\n    <li>Can't be said</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,finite-automata",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336805",
          "text": "<p>If a random coin is tossed $11$ times, then what is the probability that for $7$th&nbsp;toss head appears exactly $4$ times?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$5/32$</li>\n    <li>$15/128$</li>\n    <li>$35/128$</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,engineering-mathematics,probability",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336804",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following is&nbsp;illegal declaration in $C$ language?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>\n    <pre class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\" data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\">\nchar*str =\"Raj is a Research scholar\";\n</pre>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n    <pre class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\" data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\">\nchar str[25] =\"Raj is a Research scholar\";\n</pre>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n    <pre class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\" data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\">\nchar str[40] =\"Raj is a Research scholar\";\n</pre>\n    </li>\n    <li>\n    <pre class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-c_cpp\" data-pbcklang=\"c_cpp\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\">\nchar[]str =\"Raj is a Research scholar\";</pre>\n\n    <p>&nbsp;</p>\n    </li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,programming-in-c,pointers,array-of-pointers",
          "category": "Programming in C"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336803",
          "text": "<p>When we use slow-start algorithm, the size of the congestion window increases _______ until it reaches a threshold.</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Additively</li>\n    <li>Multiplicatively</li>\n    <li>Exponentially</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,congestion-control,sliding-window",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336802",
          "text": "<p>If $X, Y$ and $Z$ are three exhaustive and mutually exclusive events related with any experiment and the $P\\left(X \\right)=0.5P\\left(Y \\right)$ and $P\\left(Z \\right)$ &nbsp;= $0.3P\\left(Y \\right)$. Then $P\\left(Y \\right)$ = ___________ .</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$0.54$</li>\n    <li>$0.66$</li>\n    <li>$0.33$</li>\n    <li>$0.44$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,engineering-mathematics,probability",
          "category": "Probability"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336801",
          "text": "<p>In $IPv4$ Addresses, classfull addressing is replaced with :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Classless Addressing</li>\n    <li>Classfull Addressing</li>\n    <li>Subnet Advertising</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,ip-addressing,ip-addressing",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336800",
          "text": "<p>An Ethernet destination address $07-01-12-03-04-05$ is :&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Unicast address</li>\n    <li>Multicast address</li>\n    <li>Broadcast address</li>\n    <li>All of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,network-addressing",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336799",
          "text": "<p>The open file table has a/an&nbsp;__________ associated with each file.</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>file content</li>\n    <li>file permission</li>\n    <li>open count</li>\n    <li>close count</li>\n</ol>",
