          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system,file-organization",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336798",
          "text": "<p>The process of loading the operating system into memory is called :&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Booting</li>\n    <li>Spooling</li>\n    <li>Thrashing</li>\n    <li>Formatting</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336797",
          "text": "<p>Why is one - time password safe ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>It is easy to generate</li>\n    <li>It cannot b shared</li>\n    <li>It is different for every access</li>\n    <li>It can be easily decrypted</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,network-security",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336796",
          "text": "<p>How many DFA's&nbsp;exits&nbsp; with two states over input alphabet $\\left \\{ 0,1 \\right \\}$</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$16$</li>\n    <li>$26$</li>\n    <li>$32$</li>\n    <li>$64$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,finite-automata,number-of-dfa",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336795",
          "text": "<p>The demerits of the fragmentation are :&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Complex routers</li>\n    <li>Open to DOS attack</li>\n    <li>No overlapping of fragments</li>\n    <li>$\\left (A \\right)$ and $\\left ( B \\right)$ both</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,computer-networks,fragmentation",
          "category": "Computer Networks"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336794",
          "text": "<p>The address field of linked list :&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Contain address of next node&nbsp;</li>\n    <li>May contain null character</li>\n    <li>Contain address of next pointer</li>\n    <li>Both $\\left (A \\right)$ and $\\left ( B \\right)$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,data-structures,linked-list",
          "category": "Data Structures"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336793",
          "text": "<p>Given two sorted list of size '$m$' and '$n$' respectively. The number of comparisons needed in the worst case by the merge sort algorithm will be :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$m^{*}n$</li>\n    <li>minimum of $m, n$</li>\n    <li>maximum of $m, n$</li>\n    <li>$m+n-1$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,algorithms,sorting,merge-sort",
          "category": "Algorithms"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336792",
          "text": "<p>Complement of $\\left (a+b \\right)^{*}$ will be :&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$Phi\\left ( \\Phi &nbsp;\\right )$</li>\n    <li>Null</li>\n    <li>$a$</li>\n    <li>$b$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,theory-of-computation,regular-expression",
          "category": "Theory of Computation"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336791",
          "text": "<p>In Boolean algebra $1+1+1+1\\dots\\dots 800$ times ones $=$ ______ .</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$1$</li>\n    <li>$0$</li>\n    <li>$11$</li>\n    <li>$800$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,digital-logic,boolean-algebra",
          "category": "Digital Logic"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336790",
          "text": "<p>In a particular system it is observed that, the cache performance gets improved as a result of increasing the block size of the cache. The primary reason behind this is :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Programs exhibits temporal locality</li>\n    <li>Programs have small working set</li>\n    <li>Read operation is frequently required rather than write operation</li>\n    <li>Programs exhibits spatial locality</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system,cache-memory",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336789",
          "text": "<p>Starvation can be avoided by which of the following statements:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:lower-roman\" type=\"i\">\n    <li>By using shortest job first resource allocation policy .</li>\n    <li>By using first come first serve resources allocation policy.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>(i) only</li>\n    <li>(i) and (ii) only</li>\n    <li>(ii) only</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "C",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system,process-scheduling",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336788",
          "text": "<p>Page fault frequency in an operating system is reduced when the :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Process tend to be I/O&nbsp;bound</li>\n    <li>Locality of reference is applicable to the process</li>\n    <li>Size of pages is reduced</li>\n    <li>Processes tend to be CPU&nbsp;bound</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "B",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,operating-system,page-fault",
          "category": "Operating System"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336787",
          "text": "<p>The expression $5-2-3*5&nbsp;–&nbsp;2$ will evaluate to $18$, if :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$‘ – ‘$ is left associative and $‘*‘$ has precedence over $‘ – ‘$</li>\n    <li>$‘ – ‘$ is&nbsp; right&nbsp;&nbsp;associative and $‘*‘$ has precedence over $‘ – ‘$</li>\n    <li>$‘ – ‘$ is&nbsp; right&nbsp;&nbsp;associative and $‘ – ‘$ has precedence over $‘*‘$</li>\n    <li>$‘ – ‘$ is&nbsp; left&nbsp; associative and $‘ – ‘$ has precedence over $‘*‘$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "nielit2017dec-assistanta,data-structures,operator-precedence",
          "category": "Data Structures"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "336786",
          "text": "<p>Finite automata requires minimum ____________ number of stacks.</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>$1$</li>\n    <li>$0$</li>\n    <li>$2$</li>\n    <li>None of the options</li>\n</ol>",
